{
  "type": "user",
  "message": {
    "role": "user",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. **Primary Request and Intent**\n   - Solve GitHub issue https://github.com/linksplatform/Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets/issues/107.\n     - Working directory: /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1791131286882.\n     - Branch: issue-107-bce58c21006b.\n   - Draft PR #108 already exists. Update it with `gh pr edit` and never create a new PR.\n   - Push only to issue-107-bce58c21006b. Make atomic commits and run local checks before pushing.\n   - When finishing:\n     - Merge main if needed.\n     - Make sure CI passes.\n     - Check the latest issue and PR comments.\n     - Update the PR description in the style of merged PR #106.\n     - Run `gh pr ready 108`.\n   - Put experiments in ./experiments and examples in ./examples.\n   - Git user is konard.\n   - **Security constraint:** the user's email (link.assistant.team@proton.me) may be used only to identify the user, for example for authorship. It must never be sent to unrelated services (request header, URL or payload) unless the user explicitly asks.\n   - **Issue #107 requirements:**\n     - README results generated exactly in this hierarchy:\n       ```\n       Doublets vs SQLite as storage for links\n         Rust doublets vs SQLite\n           32 bit address/id space benchmarks\n           64 bit address/id space benchmarks\n         C# doublets vs SQLite\n           32 bit\n           64 bit\n       Doublets vs SQLite as storage for objects\n         (same Rust/C# × 32/64 structure)\n       ```\n     - SQLite table `links(id, from, to)` with the obvious indices, and the same id type in C# and Rust.\n     - Fully symmetrical, even coverage.\n     - Object benchmarks with and without a sequences cache, in all languages.\n     - All dependencies at their latest versions.\n     - Short, self-explanatory code with few comments.\n     - No false positives or false negatives.\n     - Fit the largest data sizes possible (100k, 1M, 10M, 100M) within the 6-hour CI limit, splitting CI per benchmark if needed.\n     - Fewer repetitions at larger sizes; more at 100k, \"but not too much, so we don't waste resources\".\n     - Follow best practices and the most common way to use SQLite and Doublets in each language.\n     - \"Make it perfect, please.\"\n\n2. **Key Technical Concepts**\n   - **Rust (already committed in 229ae26)**\n     - Uses doublets 0.5.0 (stable, edition 2024) and rusqlite 0.40.2 (bundled, fallible_uint).\n     - Same lifecycle, harness and JSON format as the C# side.\n   - **Split store bug in doublets 0.5.0 (Rust)**\n     - Updating a link so it references itself corrupts the split store; a later delete panics.\n     - Workaround: update to (0, 0) first. Documented in experiments/split_store_delete.\n   - **C# packages**\n     - net10.0, Microsoft.Data.Sqlite 10.0.12, Platform.Data.Doublets 0.18.1, Platform.Data.Doublets.Sequences 0.6.5.\n     - Transitive dependencies include Platform.Data 0.16.1 and Platform.Memory 0.4.1.\n     - Generic math constraints: `T : struct, IBinaryInteger<T>, IUnsignedNumber<T>, IMinMaxValue<T>`.\n   - **C# Doublets API (checked by reflection)**\n     - `UnitedMemoryLinks<T>(IResizableDirectMemory)` and `SplitMemoryLinks<T>(data, index)`.\n     - Memory types: `HeapResizableDirectMemory` and `FileMappedResizableDirectMemory(path)`.\n     - Extension methods: CreateAndUpdate, Create, CreatePoint, Update(link, s, t), Delete, Exists, GetLink, SearchOrDefault (returns 0 when not found), `Each(ReadHandler, params T[])`, `Count(params T[])`, SingleOrDefault(IList), GetOrCreate.\n     - `ReadHandler<T>` is `T(IList<T>?)` and returns `Constants.Continue` or `Constants.Break`.\n     - `PropertiesOperator<T>`:\n       - GetValue does SearchOrDefault(obj, prop), then `SingleOrDefault(new Link<T>(any, objectProperty, any))`, then GetTarget(GetIndex(valueLink)).\n       - SetValue does GetOrCreate(obj, prop), then `DeleteMany(AllIndices(any, objectProperty))`, then GetOrCreate(objectProperty, value).\n     - SingleOrDefault returns null when it finds more than one match. Its handler stores the `link` reference.\n   - **Microsoft.Data.Sqlite transactions**\n     - When a transaction is pending, every command must have `.Transaction` set.\n     - A command whose Transaction refers to a stale (disposed) transaction throws outside the transaction, so it must be reset to null afterwards.\n   - **Sizing results (local machine: 6 CPUs, 11 GB RAM)**\n     - Links 64-bit, all 6 Rust variants: 100k takes 16 s per repetition; 1M takes 298 s per repetition.\n     - At 1M, United Doublets is slow: update about 18 µs and from_to search about 2.5 µs. Split create is 0.8–0.9 µs. SQLite_File update is 59 µs.\n     - Plan:\n       - Links at 100k, 1M and 10M, with one job per language × bits × size. 10M is estimated at about 1–1.5 h per repetition.\n       - 100M is excluded by default (time over 6 h, memory and disk) and documented; possibly allow it via a workflow_dispatch `sizes` input.\n       - Objects likely at 10k, 100k and 1M.\n     - Repetitions: `clamp(work / size, 1, 10)` with DEFAULT_WORK = 3M. This gives 100k → 10, 1M → 3, 10M → 1. Already implemented in C# Program.cs; rust/src/main.rs still needs the same change (currently `DEFAULT_WORK = 10_000_000` with `.max(1)`).\n\n3. **Files and Code Sections**\n   - **Removed with `git rm`:**\n     - All legacy C# files: Benchmarks.cs, Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets.csproj, Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets.sln, Doublets/, Links/, LinksBenchmarks.cs, LinksSelfTest.cs, Model/, Program.cs, SQLite/, SizeAfterCreationColumn.cs, TestRun.cs, TestRunResults.cs, out.py, results.md, test_out.py.\n     - csharp/.gitignore remains.\n   - **csharp/global.json:** sdk version 10.0.100, rollForward latestFeature, allowPrerelease false.\n   - **csharp/SQLiteVSDoublets/SQLiteVSDoublets.csproj**\n     - Exe, net10.0, ImplicitUsings, Nullable.\n     - RootNamespace Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets; AssemblyName sqlite-vs-doublets.\n     - TreatWarningsAsErrors and InvariantGlobalization enabled.\n     - PackageReferences: Microsoft.Data.Sqlite 10.0.12, Platform.Data.Doublets 0.18.1, Platform.Data.Doublets.Sequences 0.6.5.\n   - **csharp/SQLiteVSDoublets/Dataset.cs**\n     - Mirrors rust dataset.rs: SplitMix64, `Link(i)` returning (From, To), Mix, LinkChecksum, LinksChecksum(n, swapped), and Scattered(n) using a Gcd helper.\n     - Also: the 5 Paragraphs, `BlogPost(i)`, BlogPostsChecksum and BlogPostsByNumberChecksum.\n     - Defines `record BlogPost(string Title, string Content, ulong PublicationDate)`, whose Checksum is the sum of UTF-8 bytes of Title and Content plus the date.\n   - **csharp/SQLiteVSDoublets/SQLiteStorage.cs** (new abstract base class)\n     - Fields: `_connection` (opened with `Data Source={path};Pooling=False`), a `_commands` list and `_table`.\n     - Constructor `(path, table, schema)` runs the schema.\n     - `Command(sql, params (string Name, SqliteType Type)[] parameters)` registers the command in `_commands`.\n     - `Count()` runs `SELECT COUNT(*) FROM {table}`.\n     - `Dispose()` disposes the commands and the connection.\n     - Current Transaction implementation (needs a fix to reset Transaction to null in a finally block):\n       ```csharp\n       public TResult Transaction<TResult>(Func<TResult> work)\n       {\n           using var transaction = _connection.BeginTransaction();\n           _commands.ForEach(command => command.Transaction = transaction);\n           var result = work();\n           transaction.Commit();\n           return result;\n       }\n       ```\n   - **csharp/SQLiteVSDoublets/Links.cs**\n     - `readonly record struct Link<T>(T Id, T From, T To)`.\n     - `ILinksStorage<T> : IDisposable where T : struct` declares Create, Update, Delete, `Link<T>? Get`, `T? Search`, Each, EachWithFrom, EachWithTo, `ulong Count()`, and a default `TResult Transaction<TResult>(Func<TResult> work) => work();`.\n     - **`SQLiteLinks<T> : SQLiteStorage, ILinksStorage<T>`**\n       - Constructed through Open(path) or InMemory() (`:memory:`).\n       - Schema: `links (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, \"from\" INTEGER NOT NULL, \"to\" INTEGER NOT NULL)` with indices `links_from_to (\"from\",\"to\")` and `links_to_from (\"to\",\"from\")`.\n       - Uses prepared commands, with create done as `INSERT ... RETURNING id` via ExecuteScalar.\n       - A `With(command, params ReadOnlySpan<T>)` helper sets the parameters; a Read helper uses the data reader.\n     - **`DoubletsLinks<T>(ILinks<T> links)`**\n       - Create uses CreateAndUpdate; Update, Delete and Get (`Exists ? Link(GetLink(id)!) : null`) map directly to the API.\n       - Search uses SearchOrDefault and maps 0 to null.\n       - Each uses `links.Each(handler, query)` with `_any`.\n       - Count uses `ulong.CreateChecked(links.Count())`; Dispose calls `(links as IDisposable)?.Dispose()`.\n       - Does NOT yet have a self-reference workaround in Update. Whether the C# split store has the same bug still needs testing.\n   - **csharp/SQLiteVSDoublets/Objects.cs**\n     - `IBlogPostsStorage<T>` declares Create, `BlogPost? Get`, Each(Action<T, BlogPost>), Delete, Count, and a default Transaction.\n     - **`SQLiteBlogPosts<T> : SQLiteStorage`**\n       - Table `blog_posts (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, title TEXT NOT NULL, content TEXT NOT NULL, publication_date INTEGER NOT NULL)`.\n       - Uses `INSERT ... RETURNING id`.\n     - **`DoubletsBlogPosts<T>`**\n       - The constructor creates meaningRoot with CreatePoint. Markers are created with Create followed by `Update(marker, meaningRoot, marker)`, in this order: unicodeSymbol, unicodeSequence, title, content, publicationDate, blogPost.\n       - Properties go through PropertiesOperator.\n       - Strings use StringToUnicodeSequenceConverter(links, CharToUnicodeSymbolConverter(links, addressToNumber, unicodeSymbol), BalancedVariantConverter, unicodeSequence).\n       - Strings are read back with UnicodeSequenceToStringConverter(links, RightSequenceWalker(links, DefaultStack, TargetMatcher(unicodeSymbol).IsMatched), UnicodeSymbolToCharConverter(links, numberToAddress, matcher), unicodeSequence).\n       - Both converters are wrapped in CachingConverterDecorator when cacheSequences is true.\n       - The date is stored as a single raw number.\n       - Get returns null if any property value is 0.\n       - Each collects ids via `Each(any, _blogPost, any)`.\n       - Count is `Count(any, _blogPost, any)`.\n       - **Failing Delete (line ~180 throws NRE):**\n         ```csharp\n         public void Delete(T id)\n         {\n             foreach (var property in (ReadOnlySpan<T>)[_title, _content, _publicationDate])\n             {\n                 var objectProperty = _links.SearchOrDefault(id, property);\n                 _links.Delete(_links.SingleOrDefault([_any, objectProperty, _any])![0]);\n                 _links.Delete(objectProperty);\n             }\n             _links.Delete(id);\n         }\n         ```\n   - **csharp/SQLiteVSDoublets/Harness.cs**\n     - Mirrors the Rust harness.\n     - Variant lists: LinksVariants (6) and ObjectsVariants (10); WarmUpSize is 10_000.\n     - `record struct Tally(Count, Checksum)` with Add and AddLink.\n     - `Timed` uses a Stopwatch and throws InvalidOperationException with \"{operation} returned unexpected records: ...\".\n     - LinksLifecycle runs: create, query_all, query_by_id, query_by_from_to, query_by_from, query_by_to, update (swap) with a check that every link was swapped, then delete with a check that the count is 0.\n     - ObjectsLifecycle runs: create, read_all, read_by_id, delete.\n     - `Measurement` record has a ToJson method that outputs median_ns, min_ns, max_ns and samples_ns.\n     - `Measure` runs GC.Collect plus WaitForPendingFinalizers before each repetition, uses a fresh workspace directory per repetition, discards the warm-up, and logs `\"{variant} #{rep}: ...\"` to stderr.\n     - MeasureLinks and MeasureObjects map variant names to factories using United and Split helpers. Files are named links.links, data.links, index.links, links.db and blog_posts.db.\n   - **csharp/SQLiteVSDoublets/Program.cs**\n     - CLI: `<links|objects> <32|64> <size> [--work N | --repetitions N] [--variants A,B] [--directory DIR] [--output FILE]`.\n     - Sets `DefaultWork = 3_000_000` and `MaxRepetitions = 10`.\n     - JSON fields: language \"C#\", category, bits, size, repetitions, warm_up_size, sqlite_version (from `SELECT sqlite_version()`) and results.\n   - **Not yet committed:**\n     - experiments/sizing/run.sh, which runs one repetition of every variant and writes /tmp/sizing-*.log and /tmp/sizing-*.json.\n     - All of the C# work above.\n   - **Rust files:** unchanged since commit 229ae26 (see the earlier summary for their content).\n\n4. **Errors and fixes**\n   - **CS8604 nullability error on `GetLink`:** fixed by adding `!`.\n   - **\"Execute requires the command to have a transaction object...\":** fixed with the SQLiteStorage base class, which assigns the transaction to every registered command.\n   - **\"The transaction object is not associated with the same connection object as this command\":** occurs when `storage.Each` runs outside a transaction after one has been used. Not fixed yet; the fix is to reset `command.Transaction = null` after commit, in a try/finally.\n   - **NullReferenceException in `DoubletsBlogPosts.Delete`:** `SingleOrDefault` returned null. Not fixed yet. Planned fix: get the value with `_properties.GetValue(id, property)`, then delete `_links.SearchOrDefault(objectProperty, value)` and objectProperty. Alternatively, investigate why the query matches more than one link.\n   - **Earlier errors (now fixed):** the Rust split store panic (workaround), the empty-string round trip, missing /usr/bin/time, and the blocked sleep command (use background tasks or Monitor instead).\n\n5. **Problem Solving**\n   - C# smoke results so far (n = 100 objects): SQLite works; the Doublets objects variants fail in Delete.\n   - Still to verify:\n     - Whether the C# split store mishandles updating a link to reference itself (for example via a test like the Rust one).\n     - Empty string and Unicode round trips in C#.\n   - Use the 100k objects sizing result, once available in /tmp/sizing-objects100k.out, to finalize the objects sizes.\n\n6. **All user messages**\n   - \"Issue to solve: https://github.com/linksplatform/Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets/issues/107 / Your prepared branch: issue-107-bce58c21006b / Your prepared working directory: /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1791131286882 / Your prepared Pull Request: https://github.com/linksplatform/Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets/pull/108 / Proceed.\"\n   - Security constraint (from system context): the user's email link.assistant.team@proton.me is to be used only to identify the user, such as for authorship or attribution. It must never be sent to an unrelated service (request header, URL or payload) unless the user explicitly asks.\n   - Periodic system prompts: \"The user hasn't heard from you in a while — say in a few words what you're doing, then continue.\"\n\n7. **Pending Tasks**\n   - **Fix the C# code:** reset Transaction after commit, and fix Doublets Delete.\n   - **Smoke-run every C# variant** for links (1000) and objects (100), for 32-bit and 64-bit:\n     ```\n     dotnet build SQLiteVSDoublets -c Release\n     dotnet SQLiteVSDoublets/bin/Release/net10.0/sqlite-vs-doublets.dll links 32 1000 --repetitions 1 --directory /tmp/cs-smoke --output /tmp/cs-links-32.json\n     ```\n   - **Add a C# test project** (csharp/SQLiteVSDoublets.Tests, using the latest xunit) mirroring the Rust tests:\n     - Dataset uniqueness and scattered.\n     - Every variant passes the lifecycle.\n     - Split self-reference update.\n     - A lossy storage gets rejected.\n     - Object round trip, including Unicode and an empty title.\n   - **Create a new .sln** (or .slnx) covering both projects.\n   - **Update rust/src/main.rs** to DEFAULT_WORK 3_000_000 and `clamp(work/size, 1, 10)`, with matching doc comment; then commit experiments/sizing/run.sh.\n   - **Unified Python report** (scripts/benchmark_report.py and its tests):\n     - Turn results/*.json into README.md and README.ru.md sections in the required hierarchy, with charts in docs/benchmarks.\n     - Remove references to the deleted csharp/out.py.\n   - **Workflows:**\n     - A benchmark matrix (language × bits × category × size, each job ≤ 6 h), plus a report/commit job.\n     - Rewrite rust.yml (stable; fmt, clippy, test, smoke) and CI.yml (net10.0, build, test, smoke; it currently references the removed --self-test and out.py).\n     - Add cargo to dependabot; consider removing cpp.yml.\n   - **Document** the doublets-rs split bug, the sizes that fit, and the exclusion of 100M.\n   - **Commit and push** atomically, check CI, update PR #108's title and description, then run `gh pr ready 108`.\n\n8. **Current Work**\n   - Debugging the C# smoke run of the new benchmark project.\n   - The last step was fetching the source of `SingleOrDefault` from linksplatform/Data.Doublets, saved to /tmp/ILinksExtensions.cs, to understand why `DoubletsBlogPosts.Delete` gets null.\n   - Its handler returns the first link and resets the result to null if a second match is found.\n   - The SQLite links variants also fail with the stale-transaction error, because `SQLiteStorage.Transaction` never resets `command.Transaction`.\n\n9. **Optional Next Step**\n   - Fix `SQLiteStorage.Transaction`: wrap the work in try/finally and set `command.Transaction = null` after commit.\n   - Rewrite `DoubletsBlogPosts.Delete` to find the value via PropertiesOperator logic: `var value = _properties.GetValue(id, property); _links.Delete(_links.SearchOrDefault(objectProperty, value));` (or investigate the duplicate matches).\n   - Rebuild and rerun the C# smoke loop for links (n = 1000) and objects (n = 100) at 32 and 64 bits.\n   - Then add the C# tests (including a split-store self-reference test) and continue with the pending tasks.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/box/.claude/projects/-tmp-gh-issue-solver-1791131286882/78aa02d9-2054-4be5-9990-31ae739e08df.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."
