        "type": "text",
        "text": "This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. **Primary Request and Intent**\n   - Solve GitHub issue https://github.com/linksplatform/Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets/issues/107.\n     - Working directory: /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1791131286882.\n     - Branch: issue-107-bce58c21006b.\n   - Draft PR #108 already exists. Update it with `gh pr edit` and never create a new PR.\n   - Push only to issue-107-bce58c21006b. Make atomic commits and run local checks before pushing.\n   - When finishing:\n     - Merge main if needed.\n     - Make sure CI passes.\n     - Check the latest issue and PR comments.\n     - Update the PR description in the style of merged PR #106.\n     - Run `gh pr ready 108`.\n   - Put experiments in ./experiments and examples in ./examples.\n   - Git user is konard.\n   - **Security constraint (verbatim intent):** the user's email (link.assistant.team@proton.me) may be used only to identify the user, such as for authorship or attribution. It must never be sent to an unrelated service (request header, URL or payload) unless the user explicitly asks.\n   - **Issue #107 requirements:**\n     - README results generated in this hierarchy:\n       ```\n       Doublets vs SQLite as storage for links\n         Rust doublets vs SQLite\n           32 bit address/id space benchmarks\n           64 bit address/id space benchmarks\n         C# doublets vs SQLite\n           32 bit\n           64 bit\n       Doublets vs SQLite as storage for objects\n         (same structure)\n       ```\n     - SQLite table `links(id, from, to)` with indices, and the same id type in C# and Rust.\n     - Fully symmetrical coverage.\n     - Object benchmarks with and without a sequences cache, in all languages.\n     - Latest versions of all dependencies.\n     - Short, self-explanatory code.\n     - No false positives or false negatives.\n     - The largest sizes that fit within the 6-hour CI limit (100k, 1M, 10M, 100M), splitting CI jobs if needed.\n     - Fewer repetitions at large sizes and more at 100k, \"but not too much\".\n     - Follow best practices.\n     - \"Make it perfect, please.\"\n\n2. **Key Technical Concepts**\n   - **Rust:** doublets 0.5.0 and rusqlite 0.40.2 (bundled SQLite 3.53.2). The split store has a self-reference bug, worked around by updating to (0, 0) first (see experiments/split_store_delete). Objects stores use `LinksConstants::external()`.\n   - **C# dependencies:** net10.0, Microsoft.Data.Sqlite 10.0.12 (SQLite 3.53.3), Platform.Data.Doublets 0.18.1 and Platform.Data.Doublets.Sequences 0.6.5.\n   - **C# delete:** must use `links.Delete(id, handler: null)`, which calls EnforceResetValues and then Delete. The raw `Delete(id)` leaves stale tree entries, so search fails within 7–13 links.\n   - **C# UnitedMemoryLinks trees:** the size-balanced trees (Default, SizeBalancedTree, RecursionlessSizeBalancedTree) degenerate in the objects workload. They now use `IndexTreeType.SizedAndThreadedAVLBalancedTree` for all United stores.\n   - **C# uncached reads:** about 1 ms per post, because Platform.Data's `GetLink` allocates a Setter, a delegate and a list and runs Each on every GetSource/GetTarget call. This is a genuine library cost, not a harness bug, and should be noted in the README. Rust caches both directions too, so the setups are symmetric.\n   - **Repetitions:** `clamp(work / size, 1, 10)`.\n     - Links: work 3,000,000, so 10 repetitions at 100k, 3 at 1M and 1 at 10M.\n     - Objects: work 500,000, so 5 repetitions at 100k and 1 at 1M.\n   - **Report comparison:** \"≈ same\" when the min–max ranges overlap or the medians are within NOISE = 5%. With a single sample, min = max, so the tolerance prevents false positives.\n   - **CI design:** one job per (language, category, bits, size) with all variants on the same runner.\n     - Sizes: links 100k, 1M and 10M; objects 100k and 1M. 100M is excluded because it exceeds 6 h.\n     - PRs run size 1000.\n     - The report job publishes on push.\n   - **Doublets file sizes** are the preallocated mmap (64 MiB united, 80 MiB split). Document this in the README.\n   - **Bot identity for results commits:** user.email 'linksplatform@gmail.com', user.name 'LinksPlatformBencher' (the repo's existing convention).\n\n3. **Files and Code Sections**\n   - **csharp/SQLiteVSDoublets/Harness.cs** (committed in ab53110)\n     ```csharp\n     /// <summary>Objects store numbers and Unicode symbols as raw numbers, which are external references.\n     /// <remarks>\n     /// The size balanced index trees (the default) degenerate when many links share a source or a target,\n     /// which makes every blog post creation linear in the number of stored posts;\n     /// the AVL trees stay logarithmic (see experiments/csharp_objects_profile).\n     /// </remarks>\n     public static ILinks<T> United<T>(IResizableDirectMemory memory, bool external = false) where T : ... =>\n         new UnitedMemoryLinks<T>(memory, UnitedMemoryLinks<T>.DefaultLinksSizeStep, new LinksConstants<T>(external), IndexTreeType.SizedAndThreadedAVLBalancedTree);\n     ```\n   - **experiments/csharp_tree_delete/Program.cs** (committed)\n     - Header documents the results table: no flags 7/13, `--self` 8/10, `--reset` and `--self --reset` no failure up to 151.\n     - Seeds two points with `Enumerable.Range(3, 149)`.\n     - Disposes each store with `using var disposable = (IDisposable)links;`.\n   - **experiments/csharp_objects_profile/Program.cs** (committed)\n     - Usage: `<united|split> <n> [tree type] [internal]`.\n     - Header lists the mean time of the marker update, for posts 1..1,000 → 9,001..10,000:\n\n       | Store | First 1,000 posts | Last 1,000 posts |\n       |---|---:|---:|\n       | United Default | 27 µs | 322 µs |\n       | United SizeBalancedTree | 82 µs | 369 µs |\n       | United RecursionlessSizeBalancedTree | 47 µs | 742 µs |\n       | United AVL | 22 µs | 2.2 µs |\n       | Split | 0.9 µs | 0.2 µs |\n\n     - With `internal` constants it degenerates the same way.\n   - **experiments/csharp_united_hub:** deleted (superseded).\n   - **scripts/benchmark_report.py** (committed in 40e676b)\n     - Full structure as before: TEXT en/ru, load, baseline, duration, size, file_size, comparison, table, provenance, chart_name, section, replace_section, charts and main.\n     - Added `NOISE = 0.05`, with `comparison` returning \"≈ same\" if the ranges overlap or the ratio is below 1 + NOISE.\n     - Markers are `<!--BENCHMARK_RESULTS_START-->` and `<!--BENCHMARK_RESULTS_END-->`.\n     - Usage: `benchmark_report.py RESULTS_DIR [--readme README.md] [--readme README.ru.md] [--charts DIR]`. Without `--readme` it prints the English section.\n   - **scripts/test_benchmark_report.py** (committed): 14 unittest tests covering formatting, Russian plurals, comparisons, noise, table, heading hierarchy, missing groups, provenance, chart links, replace_section, duplicate rejection, and main end-to-end (skipped without matplotlib).\n   - **scripts/requirements.txt:** `matplotlib==3.11.2`.\n   - **rust/src/main.rs and csharp/SQLiteVSDoublets/Program.cs** (committed in 105f9a6)\n     - `LINKS_WORK`/`LinksWork` = 3_000_000 and `OBJECTS_WORK`/`ObjectsWork` = 500_000.\n     - Doc comment: \"Objects get less work, because one blog post takes hundreds of links.\"\n     - CLI: `sqlite-vs-doublets <links|objects> <32|64> <size> [--work N | --repetitions N] [--variants A,B] [--directory DIR] [--output FILE]`.\n     - JSON output fields: language, category, bits, size, repetitions, warm_up_size, sqlite_version, and results[{variant, file_bytes, operations{op: {median_ns, min_ns, max_ns, samples_ns}}}].\n   - **.github/workflows/rust.yml** (rewritten, uncommitted)\n     - Triggers: push to main and pull_request, with paths rust/** and the workflow file.\n     - Matrix: ubuntu, macos and windows.\n     - Uses checkout@v7, dtolnay/rust-toolchain@stable (rustfmt, clippy) and Swatinem/rust-cache@v2 (workspaces: rust).\n     - Runs `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --release --all-targets -- -D warnings` and `cargo test --release`.\n   - **.github/workflows/csharp.yml** (new; CI.yml was removed with `git rm`)\n     - Matrix: 3 OSes.\n     - Uses setup-dotnet@v6 with `global-json-file: csharp/global.json`.\n     - Runs `dotnet build -c Release -warnaserror` and `dotnet test --project SQLiteVSDoublets.Tests -c Release --no-build`.\n   - **.github/workflows/benchmarks.yml** (new, uncommitted)\n     - Triggers:\n       - push to main and pull_request, with paths rust/**, csharp/**, scripts/** and the workflow file;\n       - workflow_dispatch with input `sizes` (default `'[100000, 1000000, 10000000]'`).\n     - Concurrency: cancel only for PRs.\n     - Jobs:\n       - `report-tests`: Python 3.13, `pip install -r scripts/requirements.txt`, `python -m unittest discover -s scripts -v`.\n       - `benchmark`:\n         - timeout-minutes 355.\n         - Matrix: language [rust, csharp] × category [links, objects] × bits [32, 64] × `size: ${{ fromJSON(inputs.sizes || (github.event_name == 'pull_request' && '[1000]') || '[100000, 1000000, 10000000]') }}`, excluding objects at 10000000.\n         - Builds Rust or C#, then sets `BENCHMARK` in GITHUB_ENV.\n         - Runs `$BENCHMARK category bits size --directory $RUNNER_TEMP/storage --output $RUNNER_TEMP/measured.json`.\n         - Uses jq to add run_url, date and machine (OS PRETTY_NAME, lscpu model, nproc cores, GiB RAM) into `results/$name.json`.\n         - Uploads the artifact `results-$NAME` with upload-artifact@v7.\n       - `report`:\n         - needs report-tests and benchmark; `if: ${{ !cancelled() && needs.report-tests.result == 'success' }}`; permissions contents: write.\n         - Checks out the ref (sha on PR, ref_name otherwise).\n         - Runs download-artifact@v8 with pattern results-* and merge-multiple, into `$RUNNER_TEMP/results` on PR or docs/benchmarks/results otherwise.\n         - On PR: prints the report to GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY.\n         - On push: runs `benchmark_report.py docs/benchmarks/results --readme README.md --readme README.ru.md --charts docs/benchmarks`, then git config as the bot, adds and commits 'Update benchmark results [skip ci]', and pushes with a pull --rebase retry loop (3 attempts).\n   - **.github/dependabot.yml** (uncommitted)\n     - nuget for /csharp (daily, limit 10).\n     - cargo for /rust (daily, limit 10).\n     - github-actions for / (weekly).\n   - **README.md** (225 lines, being read)\n     - Line 1 has the CI badge (workflows/CI), which needs updating because CI.yml was removed.\n     - Lines 11–86 contain the old \"Automated benchmark suite\" section, stale local run instructions, and the CSHARP_/RUST_ marker sections with old tables and charts (docs/benchmarks/bench_*.png). These must be replaced.\n     - Lines 88+ contain the historical SQLite/Doublets code and the old Result/Conclusion sections. Keep these.\n     - README.ru.md (226 lines) has the parallel structure.\n\n4. **Errors and fixes**\n   - **csharp_tree_delete `--reset` \"hang\":**\n     - Generator infinite loop at n = 2 → seeded with two points.\n     - OOM kill (exit 137) because stores were never disposed (native HeapResizableDirectMemory) → added a `using` dispose.\n     - A capped GC heap didn't help, which showed the memory was native.\n   - **actionlint:** reported only the legacy `checkout@v1`/`@v2` in AutoMerge.yml and cpp.yml. Those were left unchanged as out of scope; the new workflows are clean.\n   - **Earlier session errors** (stale transaction, NullReferenceException on delete, AccessViolationException in split objects, VSTest on .NET 10, pkill self-match, Platform.Delegates namespace): all were fixed earlier.\n\n5. **Problem Solving**\n   - **C# objects United degeneration:** solved with AVL trees.\n   - **C# objects sizing at 100k with AVL:** still running (background task bfghh2ze0, log /tmp/cs-sizing-objects.log). Partial results (ns/op):\n\n     | Variant | create | read_all | read_by_id | delete |\n     |---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n     | SQLite_Memory | 16,022 | 4,524 | 9,625 | 11,345 |\n     | SQLite_File | 19,461 | 9,744 | 17,730 | 28,941 |\n     | United Volatile Cached | 75,661 | 64,841 | 8,028 | 52,565 |\n     | United Volatile Uncached | 439,653 | 1,003,942 | 935,420 | 67,091 |\n     | United NonVolatile Cached | 51,527 | 21,888 | 7,862 | 43,799 |\n     | United NonVolatile Uncached | 528,834 | 926,592 | 934,493 | 56,999 |\n     | Split Volatile Cached | 39,351 | 29,821 | 12,225 | 45,865 |\n\n   - **Time estimates:** C# objects take about 17–18 min per repetition at 100k, so 5 repetitions take about 1.5 h. 1M at 1 repetition is estimated at 3–4 h, which is risky but under 355 min. If it times out on CI, consider splitting or documenting.\n   - **C# links at 100k (64-bit, AVL), ns/op:**\n\n     | Variant | create | query_all | update | delete |\n     |---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n     | SQLite_Memory | 22,131 | 916 | 16,181 | 11,790 |\n     | United Volatile | 9,282 | 411 | 12,957 | 6,353 |\n     | Split NonVolatile | 1,863 | 38 | 1,618 | 1,357 |\n\n6. **All user messages**\n   - \"Issue to solve: https://github.com/linksplatform/Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets/issues/107 / Your prepared branch: issue-107-bce58c21006b / Your prepared working directory: /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1791131286882 / Your prepared Pull Request: https://github.com/linksplatform/Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets/pull/108 / Proceed.\"\n   - Security constraint (from context): the email link.assistant.team@proton.me is for identification only (authorship or attribution). Never send it to unrelated services unless the user explicitly asks.\n   - Periodic system prompts: \"The user hasn't heard from you in a while — say in a few words what you're doing, then continue.\"\n\n7. **Pending Tasks**\n   - **Commit the workflows:** rust.yml, csharp.yml, benchmarks.yml, dependabot.yml and the CI.yml removal.\n   - **Update README.md and README.ru.md:**\n     - Replace lines 11–86 (old suite description, local instructions and the CSHARP_/RUST_ marker sections) with:\n       - methodology;\n       - local run instructions (cargo/dotnet commands, `scripts/benchmark_report.py`);\n       - sizes, repetitions and the reason 100M (and 10M objects) are excluded;\n       - legend: same-durability baselines, \"≈ same\" meaning overlapping ranges or within 5%, Doublets file sizes being the preallocated mmap;\n       - known bugs and notes: the doublets-rs split self-reference bug, the C# delete overload, the external references requirement, United SBT degeneration leading to AVL trees, and C# uncached reads being slow because of GetLink allocations;\n       - a single `<!--BENCHMARK_RESULTS_START-->`/`<!--BENCHMARK_RESULTS_END-->` pair.\n     - Update the CI badge (workflows CI → Rust/C#/Benchmarks).\n     - Remove the old docs/benchmarks/bench_*.png charts.\n     - Keep the historical sections.\n     - Consider generating an initial section (\"No results yet\") with the script.\n   - **Push, then check CI.** Download logs on failure. Windows/macOS Rust and C# tests have not been verified yet.\n   - **Possibly add the branch to the benchmarks.yml push trigger temporarily**, so the full results get committed to the PR branch. Then remove the trigger.\n   - **Finish the PR:** update PR #108's title and description in the style of PR #106 (including how to reproduce and the tests), check comments, merge main if needed, and run `gh pr ready 108`.\n   - **Check the background sizing log** (/tmp/cs-sizing-objects.log) for the total time to confirm the CI budget.\n\n8. **Current Work**\n   - Just finished writing the workflows (uncommitted).\n   - Started reading README.md (lines 1–135) to restructure it.\n   - The old content to replace is lines 11–86:\n     - \"## Automated benchmark suite\";\n     - the outdated local commands (`cargo bench`, `--self-test`, BENCHMARK_LINK_COUNT);\n     - \"### C# link results\" with CSHARP markers;\n     - \"### Rust link and object results\" with RUST markers;\n     - \"The original C# object comparison and its historical results remain below.\"\n   - Line 1's badge points to workflows/CI.\n\n9. **Optional Next Step**\n   - Commit the workflow changes. Example message: \"CI: stable Rust and .NET 10 checks, benchmark matrix that publishes README results; dependabot for cargo and actions\".\n   - Then rewrite the README.md and README.ru.md benchmark sections (lines 11–86) as described in Pending Tasks, with a single marker pair. Run `python3 scripts/benchmark_report.py <dir> --readme README.md --readme README.ru.md` against an empty or sample directory to verify the markers.\n   - Then push and monitor CI for PR #108.\n</summary>\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/box/.claude/projects/-tmp-gh-issue-solver-1791131286882/78aa02d9-2054-4be5-9990-31ae739e08df.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."
