  "type": "user",
  "message": {
    "role": "user",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. **Primary Request and Intent**\n   - Solve GitHub issue https://github.com/linksplatform/Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets/issues/107.\n     - Working directory: /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1791131286882.\n     - Branch: issue-107-bce58c21006b.\n   - Draft PR #108 already exists. Update it with `gh pr edit` and never create a new PR.\n   - Push only to issue-107-bce58c21006b. Make atomic commits and run local checks before pushing.\n   - When finishing:\n     - Merge main if needed (currently no new main commits).\n     - Make sure CI passes.\n     - Check the latest issue and PR comments (none so far).\n     - Update the PR description in the style of merged PR #106 (sections: What changed, Reproduction and regression coverage, Verification, no-UI note).\n     - Run `gh pr ready 108`.\n   - Put experiments in ./experiments and examples in ./examples. Git user is konard.\n   - **Security constraint (verbatim intent):** the user's email (link.assistant.team@proton.me) may be used only to identify the user, such as for authorship or attribution. It must never be sent to an unrelated service (request header, URL or payload) unless the user explicitly asks.\n   - **Issue #107 requirements:**\n     - README results in this hierarchy: category (links/objects) → language (Rust/C#) → 32/64 bit → size.\n     - SQLite `links(id, from, to)` with indices, and the same id type in both languages.\n     - Fully symmetrical coverage.\n     - Objects benchmarks with and without a sequences cache.\n     - Latest dependencies.\n     - Short, self-explanatory code.\n     - No false positives or false negatives.\n     - The largest sizes that fit within the 6-hour CI limit (100k, 1M, 10M, 100M), splitting jobs if needed.\n     - Fewer repetitions at large sizes and more at small sizes.\n     - Best practices. \"Make it perfect, please.\"\n\n2. **Key Technical Concepts**\n   - **Rust dependencies:** doublets 0.5.0 and rusqlite 0.40.2 (SQLite 3.53.2).\n     - The split store has a self-reference bug, worked around by updating to (0, 0) first.\n     - Objects stores use `LinksConstants::external()`.\n   - **C# dependencies:** net10.0, Microsoft.Data.Sqlite 10.0.12 (SQLite 3.53.3), Platform.Data.Doublets 0.18.1 and Sequences 0.6.5.\n     - Delete with `Delete(id, handler: null)`.\n     - United stores use `IndexTreeType.SizedAndThreadedAVLBalancedTree`.\n     - Uncached reads go through the library's UnicodeSequenceToStringConverter and RightSequenceWalker. They cost about 1.2 ms per post locally (a library cost, kept as is).\n   - **Repetitions:** `clamp(work / size, 1, 10)`, with links work 3,000,000 and objects work 500,000. The warm-up uses min(n, 10,000).\n   - **Report comparison:** now uses **interquartile ranges** (`statistics.quantiles(n=4, method=\"inclusive\")`; a single sample gives (x, x)). \"≈ same\" if the IQRs overlap or the medians are within NOISE = 5%.\n   - **CI runner:** Ubuntu 24.04.5, AMD EPYC 7763, 4 cores, 16 GiB. It is about 2.5× faster than the local machine (median CI/local ratio 0.39).\n     - C# objects at 100k: 21 min per repetition locally, so about 8.5 min on CI. 1M is estimated at about 1.5 h on CI.\n     - Rust links at 1M cost about 290 µs per link across all variants locally, so 100M as a single job likely exceeds 6 h.\n     - Decision: keep one job per table (same-machine comparisons). 100M links and 10M objects are excluded.\n   - **Workflows not yet on main** are listed under their file name (e.g. \"csharp\") until merged.\n\n3. **Files and Code Sections**\n   - **.github/workflows/benchmarks.yml, rust.yml, csharp.yml, dependabot.yml; CI.yml removed** (committed in 4d83c84).\n     - benchmarks.yml (full content was shown earlier):\n       - Jobs: report-tests, a benchmark matrix (language × category × bits × size, excluding objects at 10000000, timeout 355) and a report job (publishes on push as LinksPlatformBencher with linksplatform@gmail.com, using a pull --rebase retry).\n     - Commit b8c842e changed line 8 to `branches: [main, issue-107-bce58c21006b]`. **This is temporary and must be reverted to `[main]`** after the full run publishes results.\n   - **README.md / README.ru.md** (committed in 48d7fa0):\n     - Line 1 has three badges (Rust rust.yml, C# csharp.yml, Benchmarks benchmarks.yml).\n     - \"## Benchmarks\" / \"## Тесты производительности\" covers:\n       - libraries;\n       - the links and objects workloads (schemas, operations, Cached/Uncached);\n       - storages and same-durability baselines;\n       - methodology (fresh store, warm-up, scattered order, checksum validation, repetitions formula, IQR + 5% rule, preallocated file sizes);\n       - CI sizes (links 100k/1M/10M, objects 100k/1M; larger sizes don't fit 6 h);\n       - local run commands (`mkdir -p results`, `cargo run --release --manifest-path rust/Cargo.toml -- links 64 100000 --output results/links-rust-64-100000.json`, `dotnet run -c Release --project csharp/SQLiteVSDoublets -- objects 32 1000 --variants SQLite_File,Doublets_Split_NonVolatile_Cached`, `python3 scripts/benchmark_report.py results`);\n       - notes (doublets-rs split bug, C# delete overload, AVL trees, external references, slow uncached C# reads).\n     - Then the `<!--BENCHMARK_RESULTS_START-->` … `<!--BENCHMARK_RESULTS_END-->` pair, currently with \"No results yet\" generated sections.\n     - Then \"## Original comparison\" / \"## Исходное сравнение\", with the historical headings demoted one level.\n     - All relative links were verified to exist.\n   - **docs/benchmarks/bench_*.png:** removed.\n   - **scripts/benchmark_report.py:**\n     - Added `import statistics`.\n     - New function:\n       ```python\n       def quartiles(measured):\n           \"\"\"The middle half of the samples: unlike the full range, one outlier repetition does not widen it.\"\"\"\n           samples = measured[\"samples_ns\"]\n           if len(samples) == 1:\n               return samples[0], samples[0]\n           first, _, third = statistics.quantiles(samples, n=4, method=\"inclusive\")\n           return first, third\n       ```\n     - `comparison` now does `(low, high), (reference_low, reference_high) = quartiles(measured), quartiles(reference)` and checks overlap on those.\n   - **scripts/test_benchmark_report.py** (15 tests, all passing):\n     - `measurement(median, *samples)` helper.\n     - `test_overlapping_interquartile_ranges_are_not_a_difference`:\n       - measured = (150, 90, 100, 150, 200, 300), whose quartiles are (100, 200);\n       - reference = (190, 150, 180, 190, 210, 260).\n     - `test_outlier_repetitions_do_not_hide_a_difference`: uses real C# 1,000-post read_by_id samples and expects \"5.07× faster\".\n   - **.gitkeep:** removed (2ac09f4).\n   - **rust/src/objects.rs `DoubletsBlogPosts`** (read during investigation):\n     - `new` creates meaning_root (`create_point`) and markers (create + update(marker, meaning_root, marker)).\n     - `sequence(&mut self, string)` does `get_or_create(AddrToRaw.convert(char), unicode_symbol)` per UTF-16 unit, then `balanced_variant` (pairwise `get_or_create`), then `get_or_create(balanced, unicode_sequence)`, with an optional cache.\n     - `walk` and `string` read the sequence back.\n   - **rust/src/harness.rs `measure_objects`:** opens `unit::Store::<T, _>::with_constants(Global::new() | mapped(dir,\"links.links\"), LinksConstants::external())` and the split equivalents.\n\n4. **Errors and fixes**\n   - **Report false negative:** min–max overlap made a 5× difference read as \"≈ same\" at 1,000 C# posts. Fixed with the IQR overlap rule.\n   - **Test fixture error:** the samples didn't include the median, so the quartiles were (97.5, 225). Fixed the fixture.\n   - **`git add docs` failed** (the directory was gone after `git rm`). Added paths without docs, since the deletions were already staged.\n   - **`sleep` followed by a command was blocked.** Used background until-loops instead.\n   - **Downloading job logs:** `gh run view --log` fails while the run is in progress, and `gh api …/logs` refuses escape sequences. Used curl with the redirect location (`curl -sI` with an auth header, then `curl` the Location URL; this sends only the gh token, not the user email).\n   - **CURRENT bug: Rust objects 1M jobs failed on CI** (jobs 111502160295 for 32 bit and 111502160318 for 64 bit; logs in ci-logs/):\n     - Both happened after SQLite finished, in the first Doublets variant (Doublets_United_Volatile_Cached).\n     - The panic was `doublets-0.5.0/src/mem/unit/generic/sources_recursionless_size_balanced_tree.rs:231:19: index out of bounds: the len is 1040384 but the index is 1040384` (inside `get_link`/`get_mut_link`, which index `self.base.mem` by link id).\n     - Local reproduction (`RUST_BACKTRACE=1 rust/target/release/sqlite-vs-doublets objects 64 1000000 --repetitions 1 --variants Doublets_United_Volatile_Cached --directory /tmp/repro`, log in /tmp/repro/log.txt) panicked within 1.9 s with `doublets-0.5.0/src/mem/unit/store.rs:153:55: Data part should be in data memory`.\n     - Backtrace: `Store<u64, Global<LinkPart<u64>>>::update_links` ← `DoubletsBlogPosts::sequence` ← `measure_objects`.\n     - Note that the 100k objects runs pass, and 1,040,384 = 127 × 8192 is the same len for both 32 and 64 bit.\n\n5. **Problem Solving**\n   - **Root cause of the 1M Rust objects panic: not yet determined.**\n     - It fails very early (within about 2 s locally, so likely during the 10k warm-up or the first posts of the 1M repetition), even though 100k works.\n     - Hypotheses:\n       - Something in the dataset or the code depends on n.\n       - A raw value (e.g. a large char or number, or the publication date) is treated as a link id.\n       - The tree memory pointer goes stale after the store grows.\n       - An unchecked growth step in doublets 0.5.0.\n     - Next: check whether the panic happens in the warm-up or in the measured repetition, and inspect `dataset::blog_post(i)` for n-dependence (e.g. content length or characters that depend on i or n).\n     - Then write a minimal experiment in experiments/ (e.g. experiments/united_store_growth), find a workaround (as with split_store_delete), and document it in the README notes.\n     - Check whether the split stores fail at 1M as well.\n   - **Full benchmark run 37224809082 status when last checked:**\n     - Succeeded: rust links 32/64 100k, rust links 32 1M, rust objects 32 100k, csharp links 32/64 100k.\n     - Failed: rust objects 32/64 1M.\n     - The others were in progress (C# objects 100k/1M, links 1M/10M).\n     - The report job will publish whatever succeeded to the branch (commit \"Update benchmark results [skip ci]\"), with results stored in docs/benchmarks/results.\n\n6. **All user messages**\n   - \"Issue to solve: https://github.com/linksplatform/Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets/issues/107 / Your prepared branch: issue-107-bce58c21006b / Your prepared working directory: /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1791131286882 / Your prepared Pull Request: https://github.com/linksplatform/Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets/pull/108 / Proceed.\"\n   - Security constraint (from context): the email link.assistant.team@proton.me is for identification only (authorship or attribution). Never send it to unrelated services unless the user explicitly asks.\n   - (Periodic system prompts asked for brief status updates. There was no other user feedback.)\n\n7. **Pending Tasks**\n   - Find the root cause of, and fix or work around, the doublets 0.5.0 united-store panic in Rust objects at 1M. Add an experiment and a regression test if feasible, plus a README note (en and ru).\n   - Wait for full run 37224809082 (background task bzo3f6ggl writes job durations to /tmp/claude-1001/-tmp-gh-issue-solver-1791131286882/78aa02d9-2054-4be5-9990-31ae739e08df/tasks/bzo3f6ggl.output). Then:\n     - inspect the failures and durations, especially C# objects 1M and links 10M;\n     - verify the published README results and charts on the branch (`git pull` first, since the bot commits to the branch).\n   - After the fix, rerun the full benchmarks (a push to the branch with the temporary trigger) so all tables are published. Then **revert benchmarks.yml line 8 to `branches: [main]`**.\n   - Decide whether 100M links fits, based on the actual 10M job durations, and update the README text if needed.\n   - Update the PR #108 title and description (PR #106 style):\n     - What changed.\n     - Reproduction and regression coverage: the split self-reference bug, the C# delete, AVL degeneration, the united growth panic, and the report false negative.\n     - Verification: cargo fmt/clippy/test (7 tests), dotnet build -warnaserror plus 28 tests, 15 Python tests, CI on 3 OSes, and the full benchmark run URL.\n     - No UI.\n   - Final checks: merge main if needed, CI green, comments checked, `git status` clean, review `gh pr diff`, then `gh pr ready 108`.\n\n8. **Current Work**\n   - Investigating the Rust objects 1M failure from full benchmark run 37224809082.\n   - The last action read `measure_objects` in rust/src/harness.rs and `DoubletsBlogPosts` in rust/src/objects.rs, after reproducing locally:\n     ```\n     thread 'main' panicked at .../doublets-0.5.0/src/mem/unit/store.rs:153:55:\n     Data part should be in data memory\n        3: <doublets::mem::unit::store::Store<u64, platform_mem::Global<...LinkPart<u64>>> as doublets::data::traits::Links<u64>>::update_links\n        4: <sqlite_vs_doublets::objects::DoubletsBlogPosts<u64, ...>>::sequence\n        5: sqlite_vs_doublets::harness::measure_objects::<u64>\n     real 0m1.937s\n     ```\n   - On CI the panic was `sources_recursionless_size_balanced_tree.rs:231:19: index out of bounds: the len is 1040384 but the index is 1040384`.\n\n9. **Optional Next Step**\n   - Continue root-causing the doublets 0.5.0 un