    "content": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. **Primary Request and Intent**\n   - Solve GitHub issue https://github.com/linksplatform/Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets/issues/107.\n     - Working directory: /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1791131286882.\n     - Branch: issue-107-bce58c21006b.\n   - PR #108 already exists. Update it with `gh pr edit` and never create a new PR.\n   - Push only to issue-107-bce58c21006b. Make atomic commits and run local checks before pushing.\n   - When finishing:\n     - Merge main if needed (verified: main has 0 new commits).\n     - Make sure CI passes.\n     - Check the latest issue and PR comments.\n     - Update the PR title and description in the style of merged PR #106 (sections: \"What changed\", \"Reproduction and regression coverage\", \"Verification\", and a closing no-UI sentence; first line \"Fixes #107\").\n     - Run `gh pr ready 108`.\n   - Put experiments in ./experiments. Git user is konard.\n   - **Security constraint (verbatim intent):** the user's email (link.assistant.team@proton.me) may be used only to identify the user, such as for authorship or attribution. It must never be sent to an unrelated service (request header, URL or payload) unless the user explicitly asks.\n   - **Issue #107 requirements:**\n     - README results in the hierarchy category (links/objects) → language (Rust/C#) → 32/64 bit → size.\n     - SQLite `links(id, from, to)` with indices and the same id type in both languages.\n     - Fully symmetrical coverage.\n     - Objects benchmarks with and without a sequences cache.\n     - Latest dependencies.\n     - Short, self-explanatory code.\n     - No false positives or negatives.\n     - The largest sizes that fit within the 6 h CI limit (100k, 1M, 10M, 100M), splitting jobs if needed.\n     - Fewer repetitions at large sizes.\n     - Best practices. \"Make it perfect.\"\n\n2. **Key Technical Concepts**\n   - **Rust:** doublets 0.5.0, platform-mem 0.3.0, platform-data 2.0.0, rusqlite 0.40.2 (libsqlite3-sys 0.38.2, SQLite 3.53.2).\n     - Store growth: `SIZE_STEP` is 2^20 and `DEFAULT_PAGE_SIZE` is 8192.\n     - The `grow` and `resize_mem` mismatch is fixed by the `Whole` wrapper.\n     - `LinksConstants::external()` puts external values in `Hybrid::half()..=MAX`.\n   - **C#:** net10.0, Microsoft.Data.Sqlite 10.0.12, Platform.Data.Doublets 0.18.1 and Sequences 0.6.5.\n   - **Repetitions:** `clamp(work/size, 1, 10)`, with links work 3,000,000 and objects work 500,000. The warm-up uses min(n, 10,000).\n   - **Report comparison:** overlap of interquartile ranges, plus a NOISE rule of 5%.\n   - **CI runner:** about 2.5× faster than the local machine.\n   - **Workflow concurrency:**\n     - The group is `workflow-ref`, with cancel-in-progress only for pull_request. A push therefore queues behind a running push run.\n     - The report job runs only if `!cancelled()`.\n\n3. **Files and Code Sections**\n   - **rust/src/memory.rs (NEW, in commit e965c93):**\n     ```rust\n     //! Works around a `doublets` 0.5.0 and `platform-mem` 0.3.0 mismatch: stores take the slice returned by\n     //! `RawMem::grow` for their whole memory, but the memories return only the grown part. A fresh store then\n     //! sees 2^20 − 8,192 = 1,040,384 links of its 2^20 and panics with \"index out of bounds\" when it creates\n     //! more, and any later growth would leave it with an empty memory. [`Whole`] returns the whole memory.\n     use doublets::mem::{FileMapped, Global, RawMem, Result};\n     use std::{mem::MaybeUninit, path::Path};\n     pub struct Whole<M>(pub M);\n     impl<M: RawMem> RawMem for Whole<M> {\n         type Item = M::Item;\n         fn allocated(&self) -> &[Self::Item] { self.0.allocated() }\n         fn allocated_mut(&mut self) -> &mut [Self::Item] { self.0.allocated_mut() }\n         unsafe fn grow(&mut self, addition: usize, fill: impl FnOnce(usize, (&mut [Self::Item], &mut [MaybeUninit<Self::Item>]))) -> Result<&mut [Self::Item]> {\n             // SAFETY: the caller's contract is passed on unchanged.\n             unsafe { self.0.grow(addition, fill)? };\n             Ok(self.0.allocated_mut())\n         }\n         fn shrink(&mut self, cap: usize) -> Result<()> { self.0.shrink(cap) }\n         fn size_hint(&self) -> Option<usize> { self.0.size_hint() }\n     }\n     /// Memory of the volatile stores.\n     pub fn volatile<T>() -> Whole<Global<T>> { Whole(Global::new()) }\n     /// Memory of the non-volatile stores, mapped from `path`.\n     pub fn mapped<T>(path: impl AsRef<Path>) -> Whole<FileMapped<T>> { Whole(FileMapped::from_path(path).unwrap()) }\n     #[cfg(test)] mod tests { ... fn grow_returns_the_whole_memory():\n       Global grow_filled(2,1) then grow_filled(3,2) returns [2,2,2];\n       volatile() returns [1,1,2,2,2] }\n     ```\n   - **rust/src/lib.rs:** added `pub mod memory;` after `pub mod links;`.\n   - **rust/src/harness.rs:**\n     - Imports `memory::{Whole, volatile}` and `mem::FileMapped`; the Global import was removed.\n     - `fn mapped<P>(directory, name) -> Whole<FileMapped<P>> { crate::memory::mapped(file(directory, name)) }`.\n     - Every `Global::new()` was replaced with `volatile()`.\n   - **rust/tests/storages.rs:**\n     - Imports `memory::volatile`.\n     - Added:\n       ```rust\n       /// A fresh store reserves 2^20 links, so this many links make it grow once.\n       const GROWN: u64 = (1 << 20) + 1;\n       fn create_until_grown(mut links: impl LinksStorage<u32>) { creates link(i) for 1..=GROWN, asserts count == GROWN and get(id) for ids [1, 1_040_384, 1_040_385, GROWN] }\n       #[test] fn stores_keep_their_links_when_their_memory_grows() { unit::Store::new(volatile()) and split::Store::new(volatile(), volatile()) }\n       ```\n     - The test takes about 29 s in debug and is fast in release.\n     - Tests still use `Global::new()` elsewhere (round_trip, split self-reference).\n   - **experiments/unit_store_growth/** (Cargo.toml with doublets 0.5.0 and a path dependency on ../../rust plus `[workspace]`; Cargo.lock; src/main.rs):\n     - Takes `bare|whole` and creates 2^21+1 links with `create_link(1, i.min(2))`.\n     - `bare` panics at link 1,040,384 with \"Data part should be in data memory\".\n     - `whole` returns Ok(2097153).\n   - **README.md / README.ru.md:** added a note after the split_store_delete note.\n     - English: \"- The stores of doublets 0.5.0 (Rust) take the part of the memory that `platform-mem` 0.3.0 returns after growing it for the whole memory, so a store fails after 1,040,384 links; the benchmarks wrap the memory in [`memory::Whole`](rust/src/memory.rs), which returns the whole memory ([experiments/unit_store_growth](experiments/unit_store_growth)).\"\n     - The Russian equivalent was added too.\n   - **.github/workflows/benchmarks.yml:**\n     - Line 8 is currently `branches: [main, issue-107-bce58c21006b]`. **This is temporary and must be reverted to `[main]`** after the full run publishes.\n     - Matrix:\n       - sizes default to [100000, 1000000, 10000000];\n       - objects 10M are excluded;\n       - timeout is 355 minutes.\n     - The report job publishes the results as LinksPlatformBencher.\n   - **scripts/benchmark_report.py and scripts/test_benchmark_report.py:** unchanged since the earlier summary. The IQR `quartiles()` and 15 tests pass.\n\n4. **Errors and fixes**\n   - **Rust objects 1M and links 10M panics on CI.**\n     - Cause: the `RawMem::grow` / `resize_mem` mismatch.\n     - Fix: the `Whole` wrapper (commit e965c93).\n   - **`should_panic` test using bare `Global`:** debug builds abort with \"unsafe precondition(s) violated: hint::unreachable_unchecked\" (undefined behavior, non-unwinding). The test was removed and replaced by the memory unit test, with documentation in the experiment.\n   - **`sleep 500; cmd` was blocked.** Use `end=$((SECONDS+560)); until [ $SECONDS -ge $end ] || <check>; do sleep 30; done` in the foreground (timeout 600000).\n   - **Job logs:** fetched via `curl -sI` with the gh token auth header to get the Location, then `curl` that URL (sends only the gh token).\n\n5. **Problem Solving**\n   - **Local verification:**\n     - `cargo fmt --check` and `cargo clippy --release --all-targets -- -D warnings` are clean.\n     - `cargo test --release` passes 9 tests: 1 memory unit test and 8 integration tests.\n     - The experiment passes fmt and clippy.\n     - Local runs: objects 200k (4 cached Doublets variants) and links 3M (4 Doublets variants) pass.\n       - In links 3M, the united stores are about 5× slower than split, e.g. update 23 µs vs 2.4 µs. This is library behavior.\n   - **Dependabot alerts** (atty, remove_dir_all, an old libsqlite3-sys) are on main's old rust/Cargo.lock only. The PR lockfile resolves them; mention this in the PR.\n   - **100M links decision is pending.** It depends on the Rust and C# links 10M job durations.\n     - In the failed run, SQLite at 10M took about 3 min (memory) and about 10 min (file). Summed ops for SQLite file ≈ 57.5 µs per link, so 100M ≈ 1.6 h+ for that variant alone.\n     - Memory needs at 100M are about 6.4 GB per 64-bit store against 16 GB RAM. Likely still excluded; document it based on the measured durations.\n\n6. **All user messages**\n   - \"Issue to solve: https://github.com/linksplatform/Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets/issues/107 / Your prepared branch: issue-107-bce58c21006b / Your prepared working directory: /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1791131286882 / Your prepared Pull Request: https://github.com/linksplatform/Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets/pull/108 / Proceed.\"\n   - Security constraint (from context): the email link.assistant.team@proton.me is for identification only (authorship or attribution). Never send it to unrelated services unless the user explicitly asks.\n   - System prompts periodically asked for brief status updates. There was no other user feedback.